# NAAS agentic pipeline dev/test toolchain — declared floors (compile input).
# Separate from shared/pyproject.toml, which holds runtime/image deps only.
#
# This is a pip-compile INPUT — declared minimum-version floors, not exact pins.
# The fully-pinned lockfile it generates is requirements-dev.txt; regenerate that
# after editing this file (see DEPENDENCIES.md).
# naas-shared (./shared) is referenced as a local path dependency below so the
# lock also pins the runtime closure the unit tests import. It is the SOLE
# compile input — Dependabot reproduces a single-input pip-compile command from
# the lockfile header; a second positional input (e.g. shared/pyproject.toml) is
# silently dropped on regeneration, deleting the whole shared closure. The
# package itself is suppressed from the lock via --unsafe-package=naas-shared
# (an editable local path is not a portable pin); only its dependencies pin.
